# Card Scanner — env (all optional; the tool runs standalone with none of these)

# ── Cloud model keys (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Capture plane defaults to LOCAL (Ollama). These enable the cloud/egress planes.
# GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key          # server-side fallback key for Groq vision
# (Gemini key is entered in the UI settings panel, not here.)

# ── Add-to-Bridge intake (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The "Add to Bridge" button resolves a sink in this order:
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_BRIDGE_INTAKE_URL  → POST the capture envelope (platform pipeline propose)
#   2. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL + ANON_KEY → insert into the `tool_captures` quarantine table
#   3. (neither set) → localStorage outbox  [zero-infra fallback]
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BRIDGE_INTAKE_URL=http://localhost:4000/trpc/tool.intake
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_publishable_anon_key
